# Security

## Secrets

- **Never** commit `.env.local`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, or a real `SCRUNCH_API_TOKEN`.
- **Never** put real API keys or Scrunch org/brand ids in README, docs, UI placeholders, or
  `.env.example` (generic placeholders only).
- Visitor names and emails live in Firestore `tmf_scrunch_leads`, visibility briefs
  in `tmf_scrunch_reports` (one doc per website), official Scrunch PDFs in Storage/Firestore
  `tmf_scrunch_pdfs`, request logs in `tmf_scrunch_audit_events` (hashed IP), and the
  gitignored `data/leads.jsonl` fallback. Do not commit PII, and do not add analytics
  that ships it anywhere else without asking.
- Do not add a client Firestore SDK or security rules that let the browser read `tmf_scrunch_leads`
  or `tmf_scrunch_reports`. Writes go through Firebase Admin only.

## Server-only env vars

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | Powers the free AEO/GEO audit generation |
| `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` | Admin SDK — writes booth leads to `tmf_scrunch_leads` |
| `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` | Local alternative path to the service-account JSON file |
| `LEADS_ADMIN_SECRET` | Booth AE passcode for `/stand-desk` (view, add, run audits) |
| `LEADS_SUPER_ADMIN_SECRET` | Stand admin passcode — archive, hide, remove, Scrunch connect/sync |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | Email sending is disabled — reserved for a future verified sender |
| `EMAIL_FROM` | Email sending is disabled — reserved for a future verified sender |
| `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY` | Server verify for Cloudflare Turnstile on `/api/audit/generate` |
| `SCRUNCH_API_TOKEN` | Not used in v1 — reserved for a future live Scrunch check |

## Public API routes

This project is intentionally **auth-free** for visitors — a public audit tool, not an internal
admin app. Public generate must stay bot-resistant:

- `POST /api/audit/generate` — public. Requires consent, a real email, honeypot empty, Turnstile
  when `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY` is set, and in-process rate limits (IP + email). Logs every
  attempt to `tmf_scrunch_audit_events`. Keep those guards — this route calls a paid Gemini API.
- `POST /api/audit/email` and `POST /api/marketing-skills/email` — disabled (503) until a
  verified sender exists.
- `GET /api/marketing-skills` — public, read-only, serves from code (`marketing-skills-seed.ts`).
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` — public site key for the captcha widget.
- `/stand-desk` and `/api/admin/leads*` — **not public**. Gated by `LEADS_ADMIN_SECRET` (booth AE)
  or `LEADS_SUPER_ADMIN_SECRET` (stand admin) via an httpOnly cookie. Do not link this from the
  visitor nav. This is not Firebase Auth — it is a booth passcode so visitor PII is not on an
  open URL. AEs cannot archive, hide, remove, or connect/sync Scrunch. Super admin can import
  AE accounts, generate Scrunch brand settings, compare, and entity-sync.

Do not add `requireApiAuth`/Firebase auth back into the kiosk routes without also adding a real
login flow — a half-wired auth gate would just break the kiosk.

## SSRF

`src/server/audit/fetch-public-page.ts` fetches the visitor-supplied website for research. It
must keep using `isSafePublicUrl()` from `src/lib/url-safety.ts` to block localhost/private IPs.
